module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.EssentialFiniteness
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.FinitePresentation
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.LocalizationLocalization
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Smooth.Locus
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-! # Recognising a local ring as a localization of a smooth algebra

Let `A` be a Noetherian ring and let `B` be a local `A`-algebra which is essentially of finite
type. This file proves that `B` is then the localization of a *smooth* `A`-algebra as soon as it
is formally smooth over `A`:
`StacksDraft.Smooth.exists_smooth_isLocalization_of_formallySmooth`.

This is the half of Stacks 0FCW which does not use the hypothesis on the diagonal. Stacks 0FCW
assumes instead that `A → B` is a flat local homomorphism of Noetherian local rings and that the
multiplication map `B ⊗[A] B → B` is a perfect ring map, and the role of that hypothesis in the
source is exactly to produce the smoothness of `B` over `A` at the closed point — the source gets
it by a Jacobian rank computation resting on Stacks 09PV (Rodicio's theorem), proved there by
Gulliksen's method on Tate resolutions (Stacks 09PN, 09PS, 09PT, 09PU). So

> Stacks 0FCW = this file + `Algebra.FormallySmooth A B` from the perfect diagonal,

and the second summand is the whole mathematical content of 0FCW. That second summand is
`StacksDraft.Smooth.formallySmooth_of_hasProjectiveDimensionLT_diagonal`, which needs only that `B`
has finite projective dimension over `B ⊗[A] B` (a perfect diagonal gives it:
`StacksDraft.Smooth.formallySmooth_of_isPerfect_diagonal`), and Stacks 0FCW itself is
`StacksDraft.Smooth.exists_smooth_isLocalization_of_hasProjectiveDimensionLT_diagonal`, with the
source's form `StacksDraft.Smooth.exists_smooth_isLocalization_of_isPerfect_diagonal`.

## Main results

* `StacksDraft.Smooth.exists_smooth_isLocalization_of_formallySmooth`: a formally smooth,
  essentially of finite type local algebra over a Noetherian ring is a localization of a smooth
  algebra.
* `StacksDraft.Smooth.formallySmooth_of_exists_smooth_isLocalization`: the converse, over any
  base and with no finiteness hypothesis.
* `StacksDraft.Smooth.exists_smooth_isLocalization_iff_formallySmooth`: the two together. This
  certifies that formal smoothness is the *exact* pivot for Stacks 0FCW rather than a convenient
  weakening of its conclusion.

## Implementation notes

`B` lives in an arbitrary universe, while the smooth algebra produced is asked to live in the
universe of `A`. That is why the finite-type algebra of which `B` is a localization is not taken
to be `Algebra.EssFiniteType.subalgebra A B` — a subalgebra of `B`, hence in `B`'s universe — but
a quotient of a polynomial ring `MvPolynomial (Fin n) A`, isomorphic to it. This is the content of
the private `exists_atPrime_presentation`, which also upgrades the presentation from finite type
to finite presentation (`A` is Noetherian) and identifies the localizing submonoid as the prime
complement of the contraction of the maximal ideal of `B`: by
`isLocalization_primeCompl_comap_of_injective`, an element of a subring of a local ring `B` over
which `B` is generated by inverting units becomes invertible exactly when it avoids that
contraction.

With `B` so exhibited as a model of `S_q`, formal smoothness of `B` over `A` *is* `A → S` being
smooth at `q` in Mathlib's sense, since `Algebra.IsSmoothAt` is formal smoothness of a localization
at the prime and formal smoothness transports along the `A`-algebra isomorphism between any two
models. Openness of the smooth locus (`Algebra.IsSmoothAt.exists_notMem_smooth`, the source's
Lemma 07BU) then moves the smoothness off the point onto a basic open `D(g)`, and `B`, being the
localization of `S` at `q ∌ g`, is a localization of `S_g` because
`Submonoid.powers g ≤ q.primeCompl`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FCW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FCW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07BU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07BU)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

universe u v

namespace StacksDraft.Smooth

/-- A local ring `B` containing `S` as a subring, over which every element of `B` becomes a
quotient by a unit coming from `S`, is the localization of `S` at the contraction of the maximal
ideal. Only invertibility in `B` is assumed of the denominators, and over a local ring that is
precisely avoiding the contracted maximal ideal. -/
private theorem isLocalization_primeCompl_comap_of_injective {S : Type*} {B : Type*} [CommRing S]
    [CommRing B] [IsLocalRing B] [Algebra S B] (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap S B))
    (hsurj : ∀ z : B, ∃ x s : S, IsUnit (algebraMap S B s) ∧
      z * algebraMap S B s = algebraMap S B x) :
    IsLocalization ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B).comap (algebraMap S B)).primeCompl B := by
  have hmem : ∀ s : S, s ∈ ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B).comap
      (algebraMap S B)).primeCompl ↔ IsUnit (algebraMap S B s) := fun s =>
    IsLocalRing.notMem_maximalIdeal
  rw [isLocalization_iff]
  refine ⟨fun y => (hmem y).mp y.2, fun z => ?_, fun {x y} hxy => ⟨1, by rw [hinj hxy]⟩⟩
  obtain ⟨x, s, hs, hz⟩ := hsurj z
  exact ⟨⟨x, s, (hmem s).mpr hs⟩, hz⟩

/-- A local algebra essentially of finite type over a Noetherian ring is the localization at a
prime of a finitely presented algebra *in the base ring's universe*.

The prime is the contraction of the maximal ideal of `B`, and the compatibility of the two algebra
structures over `A` is part of the conclusion. -/
@[ega "IV 1.3.10" "special case"]
private theorem exists_atPrime_presentation (A : Type u) (B : Type v) [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [IsLocalRing B] [IsNoetherianRing A] [Algebra A B] [Algebra.EssFiniteType A B] :
    ∃ (S : Type u) (_ : CommRing S) (_ : Algebra A S) (_ : Algebra.FinitePresentation A S)
      (_ : Algebra S B) (q : Ideal S) (_ : q.IsPrime),
      IsScalarTower A S B ∧ IsLocalization q.primeCompl B := by
  classical
  -- `B` is a localization of the finite-type subalgebra `S₀`, which lives in `B`'s universe.
  obtain ⟨n, f, hf⟩ := Algebra.FiniteType.iff_quotient_mvPolynomial''.mp
    (inferInstance : Algebra.FiniteType A (Algebra.EssFiniteType.subalgebra A B))
  -- Replace `S₀` by an isomorphic quotient of a polynomial ring over `A`, in `A`'s universe.
  let e := Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective hf
  let φ : (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ⧸ RingHom.ker f) →ₐ[A] B :=
    (Algebra.EssFiniteType.subalgebra A B).val.comp e.toAlgHom
  let _ : Algebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ⧸ RingHom.ker f) B := φ.toRingHom.toAlgebra
  have hmap : algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ⧸ RingHom.ker f) B = φ := rfl
  have hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ⧸ RingHom.ker f) B) :=
    hmap ▸ Subtype.val_injective.comp e.injective
  have htower : IsScalarTower A (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ⧸ RingHom.ker f) B :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun a => (φ.commutes a).symm
  -- Denominators: an element of `B` is a quotient by a unit coming from the subalgebra.
  have hsurj : ∀ z : B, ∃ x s : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ⧸ RingHom.ker f,
      IsUnit (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ⧸ RingHom.ker f) B s) ∧
      z * algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ⧸ RingHom.ker f) B s =
        algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ⧸ RingHom.ker f) B x := by
    intro z
    obtain ⟨⟨x₀, s₀⟩, hz⟩ := IsLocalization.surj (Algebra.EssFiniteType.submonoid A B) z
    have hval : ∀ y : Algebra.EssFiniteType.subalgebra A B,
        algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ⧸ RingHom.ker f) B (e.symm y) = (y : B) :=
      fun y => congrArg (fun w : Algebra.EssFiniteType.subalgebra A B => (w : B))
        (e.apply_symm_apply y)
    refine ⟨e.symm x₀, e.symm s₀, ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [hval]
      exact s₀.2
    · rw [hval, hval]
      simpa using hz
  have hfp : Algebra.FinitePresentation A (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ⧸ RingHom.ker f) :=
    Algebra.FinitePresentation.of_finiteType.mp (Algebra.FiniteType.equiv inferInstance e.symm)
  exact ⟨MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ⧸ RingHom.ker f, inferInstance, inferInstance, hfp, inferInstance,
    _, inferInstance, htower, isLocalization_primeCompl_comap_of_injective hinj hsurj⟩

/-- **A formally smooth local algebra essentially of finite type is a localization of a smooth
algebra.** Let `A` be Noetherian and let `B` be a local `A`-algebra, essentially of finite type
and formally smooth over `A`. Then there is a smooth `A`-algebra `C`, in the universe of `A`, and
a submonoid `M` of `C`, such that `B` is the localization of `C` at `M` compatibly with `A`.

This is Stacks 0FCW with its hypothesis on the diagonal replaced by the formal smoothness that
hypothesis exists to provide; see the module docstring. -/
public theorem exists_smooth_isLocalization_of_formallySmooth (A : Type u) (B : Type v)
    [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsLocalRing B] [IsNoetherianRing A] [Algebra A B]
    [Algebra.EssFiniteType A B] (h : Algebra.FormallySmooth A B) :
    ∃ (C : Type u) (_ : CommRing C) (_ : Algebra A C) (_ : Algebra.Smooth A C)
      (M : Submonoid C) (_ : Algebra C B), IsScalarTower A C B ∧ IsLocalization M B := by
  obtain ⟨S, _, _, _, _, q, _, _, hloc⟩ := exists_atPrime_presentation A B
  have : IsLocalization.AtPrime B q := hloc
  -- `B` is a model of `S_q`, so formal smoothness of `B` over `A` is smoothness of `S` at `q`.
  have : Algebra.IsSmoothAt A q :=
    (Algebra.FormallySmooth.iff_of_equiv
      ((IsLocalization.algEquiv q.primeCompl B (Localization.AtPrime q)).restrictScalars A)).mp h
  -- Openness of the smooth locus moves the smoothness onto a basic open `D(g)`, `g ∉ q`.
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hsm⟩ := Algebra.IsSmoothAt.exists_notMem_smooth A q
  have hle : Submonoid.powers g ≤ q.primeCompl := Submonoid.powers_le.mpr hg
  let algCB : Algebra (Localization.Away g) B :=
    IsLocalization.localizationAlgebraOfSubmonoidLe (Localization.Away g) B
      (Submonoid.powers g) q.primeCompl hle
  have : IsScalarTower S (Localization.Away g) B :=
    IsLocalization.localization_isScalarTower_of_submonoid_le (Localization.Away g) B
      (Submonoid.powers g) q.primeCompl hle
  exact ⟨Localization.Away g, inferInstance, inferInstance, hsm,
    q.primeCompl.map (algebraMap S (Localization.Away g)), algCB,
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun a => by
      rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A S B a, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A S
        (Localization.Away g) a, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply S (Localization.Away g) B],
    IsLocalization.isLocalization_of_submonoid_le (Localization.Away g) B
      (Submonoid.powers g) q.primeCompl hle⟩

/-- A localization of a smooth algebra is formally smooth: smoothness gives formal smoothness of
`A → C`, a localization is always formally smooth over the ring it localizes, and formal smoothness
is stable under composition. -/
@[ega "0 19.3.5" "(iv), special case"]
public theorem formallySmooth_of_exists_smooth_isLocalization (A : Type u) (B : Type v)
    [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    (h : ∃ (C : Type u) (_ : CommRing C) (_ : Algebra A C) (_ : Algebra.Smooth A C)
      (M : Submonoid C) (_ : Algebra C B), IsScalarTower A C B ∧ IsLocalization M B) :
    Algebra.FormallySmooth A B := by
  obtain ⟨C, _, _, _, M, _, _, _⟩ := h
  have : Algebra.FormallySmooth C B := Algebra.FormallySmooth.of_isLocalization M
  exact Algebra.FormallySmooth.comp A C B

/-- **For a local algebra essentially of finite type over a Noetherian ring, being a localization
of a smooth algebra is exactly formal smoothness.**

This is what makes `Algebra.FormallySmooth A B` the exact pivot for Stacks 0FCW: the conclusion of
0FCW is *equivalent* to it under 0FCW's remaining hypotheses, so replacing 0FCW's hypothesis on
the diagonal by formal smoothness weakens nothing and leaves precisely one implication — the
perfect diagonal forces formal smoothness, which rests on Stacks 09PV and is
`StacksDraft.Smooth.formallySmooth_of_isPerfect_diagonal`, through finite projective dimension of
the diagonal (`StacksDraft.Smooth.formallySmooth_of_hasProjectiveDimensionLT_diagonal`). -/
public theorem exists_smooth_isLocalization_iff_formallySmooth (A : Type u) (B : Type v)
    [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsLocalRing B] [IsNoetherianRing A] [Algebra A B]
    [Algebra.EssFiniteType A B] :
    (∃ (C : Type u) (_ : CommRing C) (_ : Algebra A C) (_ : Algebra.Smooth A C)
      (M : Submonoid C) (_ : Algebra C B), IsScalarTower A C B ∧ IsLocalization M B) ↔
      Algebra.FormallySmooth A B :=
  ⟨formallySmooth_of_exists_smooth_isLocalization A B,
    exists_smooth_isLocalization_of_formallySmooth A B⟩

end StacksDraft.Smooth

end
